NAVIGATION NOTE (covenant #7 — no predecessor bypass)
  The web /locations route has no pre-existing AppRoute counterpart: .maps (pathSegment "maps") is the separate
  web MapOverview surface, and the parser alias "/location" (singular) already points at .maps. /locations
  (plural) is the LocationsPage. A NEW .locations case (pathSegment defaults to rawValue "locations") is the
  honest, minimal way to give it a real navigation home + deep link THROUGH the shared infra. Blast-radius:
    - AppRoute.swift switches exhaustively over systemImage + group — both updated for .locations (no default arm).
    - pathSegment falls through to rawValue ("locations"); AppRouteParser resolves /locations with no alias.
    - MenuCommandCatalog + SpotlightIndexer derive from AppRoute.allCases, so testNavigateCommandsCoverEveryRoute /
      testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment / testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup stay green automatically (unique
      segment, group .vehicle).
  TeslaSyncApp composes LocationsRouteRegistration.registry(.locations, onViewDrives:{ selection = .driving })
  into the existing chain; no sibling registration, the parser, or any other AppRoute case is displaced.

AI-INTEGRATION NOTE (covenant #2/#5 — faithful, not a stub)
  The web renders <AIAutoNameUnnamedLocations onApplyName=…/> per unnamed row + parks the proposal in the
  page-local `appliedName` state, showing the `locations.aiAutoName.applied` confirmation. The native parity
  embeds the REAL AIAutoNameUnnamedLocations shared surface (TeslaSync/shared-surfaces) for unnamed rows, built
  with the public InMemoryAINameDraftSource (NO networking — the same seam its own #Previews use) and onApply
  wired to LocationsPageModel.applyName, which surfaces the confirmation. The streaming AI surface is a separate
  parity unit; LocationsPage owns only the unnamed-detection (isUnnamed, ported verbatim incl. the coordinate
  regex) + the applied-name hand-off, exactly as the web page does.

